{"source":"https://claudecertificationguide.com/learn/quick-reference","rules":{
"1":[
["\"guaranteed\" / \"must always\" / \"enforce\"","Hooks (programmatic enforcement), not prompts"],
["\"flexibility\" / \"adapt\" / \"unexpected\"","Model-driven decisions"],
["\"independent subtasks\"","Parallel (multiple Task calls in one response)"],
["\"each step needs prior output\"","Sequential"],
["\"premature termination\"","Check stop_reason correctly"],
["\"runaway agent\"","Iteration cap as a safety net"],
["\"share context between agents\"","Explicit passing only — no shared memory"],
["\"complex task, unknown structure\"","Dynamic adaptive decomposition"],
["\"compliance / regulatory / audit\"","Programmatic enforcement"],
["Escalation: classifier score vs agent self-reported confidence","Classifier scores are valid triggers; self-reported confidence is not"]
],
"2":[
["Claude keeps picking the wrong tool (small toolkit)","Improve tool descriptions"],
["Claude keeps picking the wrong tool (20+ tools)","Split by role or consolidate — not descriptions"],
["Guaranteed structured output","Forced tool_choice for one known schema; tool_choice: any across multiple"],
["Model should decide whether/which tool","tool_choice: auto"],
["Must call a tool but can choose which","tool_choice: any"],
["Search returned no results","Valid empty result — accept it"],
["API returned 401 / timeout","Access failure — retry or escalate"],
["Need a custom MCP server","Check community servers first"],
["Project-wide MCP config","`.mcp.json` in project root"],
["Personal MCP config","`~/.claude.json`"]
],
"3":[
["Guaranteed enforcement, cannot be bypassed","Hooks (PreToolUse / PostToolUse) or settings"],
["Style guidance, preferred approach","Instructions in CLAUDE.md"],
["Applies only to specific file paths","`.claude/rules/` with paths frontmatter"],
["Reusable workflow with restricted tools","Skills (`.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`)"],
["Prompt template with arguments","Commands (`.claude/commands/`)"],
["CI/CD pipeline, automated, non-interactive","-p flag"],
["Extra rules but keep default coding behaviour","--append-system-prompt (not --system-prompt)"],
["Fast scripted run, skip project config/hooks/skills","--bare"],
["Machine-parseable / schema-validated CI output","--output-format json + --json-schema"],
["Review quality of generated code","Independent session (not the writing session)"],
["Multiple approaches, complex task","Plan mode first"],
["Personal preference, not shared","`~/.claude/` (user-level config)"]
],
"4":[
["Guaranteed schema compliance","Forced tool_choice with a specific tool; tool_choice: any when document type unknown"],
["Output sometimes has wrong format","Add few-shot examples (2–4)"],
["Model fabricates missing data","Make schema fields optional/nullable"],
["Validation failed, need to fix","Retry-with-error-feedback (original + failed extraction + error)"],
["50% cost reduction, bulk processing","Batch API"],
["Real-time, user-facing / blocking","NOT Batch — use synchronous API"],
["Model reviewing its own output","Separate instance (not same session)"],
["Large multi-file input, missing details","Per-file passes + cross-file integration pass"],
["Instructions alone aren't working","Add few-shot examples"]
],
"5":[
["Details lost over a long conversation","Persistent case-facts block, not progressive summarisation"],
["Findings need to survive context reset","Scratchpad files for external persistence"],
["Tool returned nothing","Distinguish valid empty (accept) from access failure (retry)"],
["High overall accuracy, users report errors","Stratified validation — check per-type accuracy"],
["Sources disagree","Annotate both with provenance and dates"],
["Generic error message received","Replace with structured error context"],
["Model contradicts itself / stale context","Fresh start with summary injection"],
["Inline citations lost after processing","Structured claim–source mappings"],
["Stable metrics but quality complaints","Track per-type error rates, not aggregates"],
["Long task exceeds context window","Scratchpad files and context boundary management"]
]
